UPDATE public.sondas_config SET question_text_en = $rsv$When you face new information that contradicts your deepest beliefs, how does your code react?$rsv$, options_json_en = to_jsonb(json_build_array(json_build_object('label',$rsv$Blind Fanaticism. My identity is my belief. If you contradict me, you attack me. I defend my ideas with anger and refuse to look at any evidence that challenges my world.$rsv$,'value',0), json_build_object('label',$rsv$Defensive Rigidity. Being wrong makes me deeply uncomfortable. I look for excuses to invalidate the new information and keep my ego intact ("being right").$rsv$,'value',25), json_build_object('label',$rsv$Conditioned Openness. I listen to different perspectives if they come from sources I respect, but it's very hard for me to publicly let go of an idea I've defended before.$rsv$,'value',50), json_build_object('label',$rsv$Agile Updating. I listen without taking it personally. If the new data is better than mine, I accept the error and rewrite my inner code with agility, without feeling humiliated.$rsv$,'value',75), json_build_object('label',$rsv$Liquid Mind. Zero attachment to form. Beliefs are just temporary tools. If a tool no longer serves, I dissolve it and adopt a higher code instantly.$rsv$,'value',100))::text) WHERE id = '75f7a925-614e-48d1-9dab-42968aa2c502';
